-- title:
--   Eigenplanes in T_λ J₀(M): eigen off the level, determinant q
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. $g$ is a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem does not occur (in the sense of the predicate `GoodEigensystemOccursAt`) at any divisor of $M$ other than $M$ itself. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals, and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the Hecke operators at primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$, for all such $\ell$. Let $O''$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a field of characteristic zero that is an $O''$-algebra, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ to $K$. Write $J_0(M)$ for the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, equipped with its module structure over $\mathbb{T}=\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ given by `heckeModuleBar`, and let $T=$ [`TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) be the $\mathbb{T}$-submodule of sequences $x:\mathbb N\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$. Assume given: a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ in which $a\cdot x$ has $n$-th entry the multiple of $x_n$ by the image of $a$ in $\mathbb{Z}/\lambda^n$; a multiplicative map $\rho_M$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (as $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ sending $a\otimes x$ to $a\otimes y$ whenever the sequence $y$ is the $\sigma$-translate of $x$; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from $\mathbb{T}$ to the same endomorphism ring with $T_M(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$; and a $K$-subspace $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ of dimension $2$, stable under the base change to $K$ of every $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which the base change of $T_M(X_\ell)$ acts by the scalar $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$. Then: (i) every $t$ in the eigen-ideal of the system $(a_\ell(g))_\ell$ — the kernel of evaluation $\mathbb{T}\to\mathbb{C}$ at these coefficients — which involves only the variables at primes not dividing $M$ annihilates $W$; and (ii) for every prime $q\ne\lambda$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^q$, the determinant of the restriction of the base change of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ to $W$ equals $q$ in $K$.
--
--   This says that any Galois-stable two-dimensional plane carrying the Hecke eigenvalues of $g$ at almost all primes is in fact the $g$-isotypic plane for the Hecke operators at all primes away from the level (a strong multiplicity one statement), and that its determinant character is the cyclotomic one, so that $W$ is a model over $K$ of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to $g$. It is the packaging used by the subsequent constructions of the residual representation and of the inertia and Frobenius information at primes dividing the level.
